+# Contract: Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [x] `create(id, content)` stores a new doc, `get(id)` returns a deep-equal copy → test: create then get returns content
+- [x] `create(id, content)` throws if `id` already exists on current branch → test: create twice throws
+- [x] `get(id)` throws if doc was never created → test: get unknown id throws
+- [x] `get(id)` throws if doc was deleted → test: create, delete, get throws
+- [x] `update(id, content)` replaces content and is visible via `get` → test: update then get returns new content
+- [x] `update(id, content)` throws if doc doesn't exist → test: update unknown id throws
+- [x] `delete(id)` removes the doc from the current branch → test: delete then get throws
+- [x] `delete(id)` throws if doc doesn't exist → test: delete unknown id throws
+- [x] Returned/stored content is deep-cloned (mutation isolation) → test: mutate object passed to create/returned from get, doesn't affect store
+
+## Version History
+- [x] `create` generates version 1; each `update` generates a new version → test: getHistory length grows
+- [x] Versions have unique `id`, a `timestamp`, and the full content at that point → test: inspect Version fields
+- [x] `getHistory(id)` returns versions oldest-first → test: timestamps/order check after several updates
+- [x] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns content of that specific version, unaffected by later updates → test: update doc, fetch old version, content matches old
+
+## Branching
+- [x] Default branch is `"main"` → test: `getBranch()` on fresh store returns `"main"`
+- [x] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state → test: create doc on main, branch, doc visible on new branch
+- [x] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from specified branch, not current → test: switch to branch A, createBranch('C', 'main') has main's state, not A's
+- [x] `switchBranch(name)` changes the active branch for subsequent ops → test: switch, create doc, doc not visible on other branch
+- [x] `listBranches()` lists all created branches including main → test: create 2 branches, list contains all 3
+- [x] Changes on one branch are isolated from another → test: update doc differently on two branches, each sees its own version
+- [x] `switchBranch`/`createBranch` with unknown source branch throws → test: createBranch from nonexistent branch throws
+
+## Merging
+- [x] Merge with no changes on either side is a no-op fast-forward: `applied: true`, empty `merged`, empty `conflicts` → test
+- [x] Change only on source branch is auto-applied to target, no conflict → test
+- [x] Change only on target branch stays as-is, no conflict, included in merged map → test
+- [x] Same field changed identically on both branches → no conflict, applied → test
+- [x] Same field changed differently on both branches → conflict recorded with correct `path`, `base`, `ours`, `theirs`; `applied: false`; target branch unchanged → test
+- [x] Nested field conflicts report dot-separated path (e.g. `"a.b.c"`) → test
+- [x] Non-conflicting fields still merge correctly alongside a conflicting field in the same document → test
+- [x] On conflict, `merged` shows the "ours"-resolved version of the document → test
+- [x] When a merge has conflicts, current branch's documents remain unchanged after `merge()` returns → test
+- [x] When merge applies cleanly, the resulting content becomes the new current content on target branch (visible via `get` and `getHistory`) → test
+- [x] Multiple independent documents changed on different branches merge cleanly together (no cross-document conflicts) → test
+- [x] Document created independently (same id) on both branches with different content → conflict at root path → test
+- [x] Document deleted on one branch, unchanged on the other → deletion applied, no conflict → test
+- [x] Document deleted on one branch, modified on the other → conflict → test
+
+## Build / Lint
+- [x] `npm run build` (tsc) succeeds with no errors
+- [x] `npm run lint` (eslint) succeeds with no errors
+- [x] `npm test` (vitest run) — all tests pass
